268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Utility models, also known as short-term patents or innovation patents, protect minor inventions that are novel and industrially applicable. The author of a utility model is granted a certificate by the Commission, giving them the exclusive right to exploit the invention and preventing unauthorized third parties from doing so.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Utility models do not protect changes in shape, proportions, or material of patented or public domain objects unless they result in an improvement in function or use. They also do not protect simple replacements of elements in known combinations that do not improve function or use, or inventions contrary to public order or morality. A utility model certificate is initially granted for five years and can be renewed for an additional five years if proof of the invention being worked in Ethiopia is provided. Industrial design refers to the visual appearance of a product that gives it a unique and distinctive look, whether through lines, colors, or three-dimensional forms. This design is focused on the external ornamental aspects of the product and does not relate to its function.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Industrial design is applied to products intended for mass production, with the design process separated from the manufacturing process. This means that the creative design of a product occurs before its physical production, which differentiates industrial design from craft-based design where the form is determined during creation.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (To apply for a patent in Ethiopia, the application must include a front page with the inventor's name, title of the invention, abstract, and diagrams. The description should cover the technical field, prior art, objective of the invention, detailed description, advantages, and application of the invention. The claim section should clearly define the protection sought in terms of technical features, pertain to product or process, be numbered consecutively, and use consistent technical terminology. Chemical or mathematical formulae may be included in the claims, but not drawings. Technology transfer involves the process of transferring knowledge, know-how, procedures, and systems related to the manufacturing and use of goods and services from one entity to another.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
