/P 175 0 R
/E (available within Ethiopian property law to outline potential future measures that can be pursued to avoid the continued destruction of historical buildings. The focus will be on the legal options and strategies that can be employed by concerned individuals and organizations to protect heritage sites in the country)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (The iconic Lombardia Restaurant, a 90-year-old establishment in Addis Ababa near the Wabi Shebelle Hotel in Lideta Sub-City, Wereda 9, has been demolished despite being legally recognized as a heritage site. The restaurant was granted heritage status on February 15, 2023, after meeting all necessary requirements. The Federal Court of First Instance issued a ruling deeming the delisting of the building as unlawful and directed the decision to the Addis Ababa City Administration Culture, Arts, and Tourism Bureau, the Federal Housing Corporation, and other relevant institutions. Despite its protected status, Lombardia Restaurant was destroyed to make room for development, with officials justifying the demolition by disputing the building's heritage designation.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (It has been well said that " the present is charged with the past and is big with the future" and that the more perfect and ordered the record of tradition is, the more the race of man becomes as one; living, learning and advancing. This two-part essay provides an overview of the legal recourse )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
