/E (The death penalty, also known as capital punishment, has been a controversial issue in Ethiopia and in the international community for many years. Some argue that the death penalty is a form of justice, while others argue that it is simply a form of revenge. In this essay, we will examine the Ethiopian legal system and international agreements to determine whether the death penalty is justice or revenge.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (In Ethiopia, the death penalty is legal under the Criminal Code of Ethiopia. The law allows for the death penalty to be imposed for a variety of crimes, including murder, terrorism, and treason. The death penalty is seen as a means of deterring crime and ensuring justice for the victims of these heinous crimes. Proponents of the death penalty argue that it serves as a form of retribution for the harm caused by the offender and provides closure for the victims' families. However, opponents of the death penalty argue that it is simply a form of revenge that fails to address the root causes of crime. They argue that the death penalty is a violation of human rights and that it is an ineffective deterrent to crime. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 178 0 R
/T ( Issue No.11/2024, Published May 16, 2024 Death Penalty: Is It Justice or Simply Revenge? by Yodit Mekuria \(yoditmekuria7@gmail.com\) )
/E ( Issue No.11/2024, Published May 16, 2024 Death Penalty: Is It Justice or Simply Revenge? by Yodit Mekuria \(yoditmekuria7@gmail.com\) )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6 600 0 R 8]
>>
endobj
