/P 179 0 R
/E (In conclusion, the death penalty remains a divisive issue in Ethiopia and in the international community. While some argue that it is a form of justice, others argue that it is simply a form of revenge. The Ethiopian legal system allows for the death penalty, but international agreements call for its abolition. Ultimately, the debate over the death penalty will continue, as societies grapple with questions of justice, human rights, and the value of human life.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
