/E (Under Article 2\(18\), the proclamation vests ECMA with the authority to list and de-list securities from an exchange. Here it must be clear that ECMA is the regulator whereas ESX is the enabler and the place where service providers meet and conduct business. In a recent documentary, the Director-General of the ECMA, Brook Taye \(Ph.D.\) used the relationship between the National Bank and Commercial Bank of Ethiopia as an analogy to compare and contrast ECMA with ESX.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
