/P 189 0 R
/E (Another indirect positive implication of the reform is the potential increase in the use of alternative dispute resolution \(ADR\). In order to avoid the high cost of formal proceedings, parties may resort to negotiation, mediation, or arbitration, which is beneficial since it will reduce the caseload on courts.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 189 0 R
/E (Despite these potential benefits, the reform poses a serious concern and downside. The major disadvantage is that the reform goes against the right of access to justice of citizens granted under Article 37 of the constitution. This provision explicitly states that everyone has the right to bring a justiciable matter to, and to obtain a decision or judgement by, a court of law or any other competent body with judicial power.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 189 0 R
/E (The revised court fee makes the judicial system financially inaccessible to a large segment of the population, in a country where most citizens struggle with limited economic means. This financial barrier could effectively deprive many citizens of their fundamental right to seek redress and protection through the courts.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
