505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (Additionally, litigants with small claims will be discouraged to bring their claims to the court due to disproportionate fees, leaving them uncompensated. For instance, litigants with claims between 0 and 20,000 birr are now required to pay 2,000 birr court fee. This creates an obvious disparity, especially for those whose claims are 2,000 birr or less, by forcing them to pay a fee that could equal or even exceed the value of their claim. This in a way contradicts with the aim of civil procedure, which stands to handle disputes in a fair and orderly manner, and as economically as possible.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
