515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (The new Commercial Code introduces a framework for protecting minority shareholders within companies. While the Code grants minority shareholders certain rights, including voting rights, mandatory buyouts, and potential board representation, it also imposes limitations that can hinder their ability to participate effectively in the company. In pretty clear expression the code cure and at the same time kill them. Thus, this legal update analyzes these protections, highlighting both their strengths and weaknesses.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 191 0 R
/T (Introduction )
/E (Introduction )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 191 0 R
/T (Safeguarding Minority Shareholders in the Code)
/E (Safeguarding Minority Shareholders in the Code)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (The new Commercial Code introduces several commendable measures designed to protect minority shareholders. A fundamental principle established is "one share, one vote." This ensures a more equitable distribution of voting power, aligning it directly with the level of share ownership held by individual shareholders. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Furthermore, the Code introduces the concept of a mandatory bid. This provision grants minority shareholders a valuable exit strategy when a single entity acquires control of the company, exceeding a threshold of 90% ownership.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Another noteworthy protection comes in the form of piercing the corporate veil. This legal principle holds majority shareholders personally liable for any abusive acts they may commit. This serves as a significant deterrent against self-dealing or other actions that prioritize the interests of majority shareholders at the expense of the company and its minority shareholders. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E ( The Code also promotes diversity within the company's decision-making body by encouraging a more balanced representation on the board of directors. This could potentially provide minority shareholders with a voice in the strategic direction of the company)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Instance of Disregard Minority Shareholders Rights)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
