528 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Only shareholders holding more than 5% of the company's capital, along with board members, supervisors, auditors, the Ministry of Trade, and courts, can call meetings. This can disadvantage minority shareholders who may lack the requisite shareholding to initiate discussions on critical matters. Similarly, the Code restricts the ability to file derivative lawsuits. These lawsuits allow shareholders to take legal action on behalf of the company for managerial misconduct when the company itself fails to act. However, only shareholders with over 10% ownership can exercise this right, potentially hindering minority shareholder effortFurther limitations exist regarding agenda-setting and meeting adjournments. Only pre-determined agendas are allowed, with the ability to add new items reserved for shareholders holding more than 5% of the shares. s to hold management accountable. This same threshold applies to the right to adjourn meetings. These restrictions can curtail minority shareholders' ability to influence the direction of meetings and address unforeseen issues. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (The new Commercial Code represents a significant step forward in recognizing and protecting the rights of minority shareholders. The principles of one share, one vote, mandatory bids, piercing the corporate veil, and encouraging board diversity offer valuable safeguards. However, limitations exist regarding the ability to call meetings, initiate derivative lawsuits, influence meeting agendas, and request.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
