570 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 196 0 R
/T (1Issue No.2/ 2024, Published April 8,2024  Preserving Ethiopia's Historic Buildings - A Heritage Worth Protecting: Part II by Nahot Girma)
/E (1Issue No.2/ 2024, Published April 8,2024  Preserving Ethiopia's Historic Buildings - A Heritage Worth Protecting: Part II by Nahot Girma)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Preserving historic structures is crucial for community cohesion, shared history, and economic growth. Promoting community participation in preservation initiatives can help preserve landmarks for future generations. Disrupting these structures undermines community pride and ownership. Preserving cultural heritage involves oral history documentation, cultural education, local artisan support, and stakeholder engagement, ensuring the survival of customs and a strong sense of identity.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
572 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 196 0 R
/T (Sentimental Values and Society)
/E (Sentimental Values and Society)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
573 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 196 0 R
/T (Legal Remedy to Arbitrary Demolition)
/E (Legal Remedy to Arbitrary Demolition)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
574 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (The Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia's Constitution provides judicial recourse in cases involving the willful destruction of historic structures. Article 41\(9\) highlights the significance of safeguarding historical and cultural treasures and protects the right to development while doing so.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Furthermore, Article 91\(2\) requires the government and every Ethiopian citizen to safeguard the nation's historical places, artifacts, and natural resources.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Legal recourse against the willful destruction of historic structures may also be pursued under Proclamation No. 209/2000, which creates the Ethiopian Authority for the study and preservation of Cultural Heritage. The proclamation's Article 4 highlights the need of preserving historical sites while outlining the goal of defending cultural heritage from man-made and natural calamities. Article 6 also gives the Authority the authority to gather data, establish guidelines for maintaining these priceless treasures, and safeguard and oversee Cultural Heritage.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
577 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Another legal remedy, if you suspect arbitrary demolition of a historical building, you can seek legal remedies through the courts, such as a lawsuit, injunction, or compensation. According to proclamation no, 574/2008, a proclamation to provide for urban plans, the initiation and preparation of urban plans must adhere to specific principles.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 196 0 R
/Pg 42 0 R
/A [1005 0 R 0]
/K [12]
>>
endobj
