582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 197 0 R
/T (| PAGE 31)
/E (| PAGE 31)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (One key principle is the preservation and restoration of historical and cultural heritages, as outlined in Article 8 of the Proclamation. This ensures that urban planning efforts prioritize the conservation of important historical and cultural assets within the urban environment.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (The Civil Procedure Code in Ethiopia provides for the granting of temporary injunctions to prevent the destruction or alienation of property, as outlined in Article 154. This remedy can be sought when historical buildings are in danger of demolition or alteration. Article 155 allows for injunctions to restrain the repetition or continuation of breaches, such as the destruction of historical buildings. In case of non-compliance, Article 156 allows for attachment of property and penalties for contempt of court. Notice to the opposite party is required under Article 157, and orders can be discharged or varied under Article 158. An injunction issued to a corporate body is binding on its officers under Article 159. As a responsible citizen, I believe that preserving historical buildings is crucial for cultural heritage and identity, and citizens should prioritize education, engage )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (with authorities, and promote sustainable development practices to prevent destruction. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
586 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (In conclusion preserving historical buildings is vital for community identity and tourism. Legal provisions in Ethiopia, such as the Constitution and Proclamation No. 209/2000, safeguard these structures. Judicial remedies, urban planning principles, and civil procedure codes offer protection against arbitrary destruction. These measures ensure the conservation of cultural heritage and provide avenues for legal action to prevent the demolition of historical buildings.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
